WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.570
<i>That sigh means he's about 
to start lecturing me.</i>

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.710
<i>He told me not to do anything unnecessary,</i>

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.110
<i>but I still think telling her 
was the right thing to do.</i>

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.030
<i>Abeno-san must've thought the same thing.</i>

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.130
<i>"That has nothing to do</i>

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>with the fact that you acted 
without my permission!"</i>

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.930
<i>...is probably what he'll say.</i>

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:09.350
<b>Mystery 7 "The Encounter"</b>

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.070
<i>Abeno-san gets violent when he's angry.</i>

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.650
<i>I should back away just in case.</i>

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.030
Thanks for today.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.780
Huh?

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.230
Whaaat?!

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:29.760
What's wrong?

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.150
What's wrong?!

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.210
That's what I'm asking you.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.960
What did you mean by "thanks for today"?

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.950
Huh? What did I mean?

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.060
You found the ring.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.820
And if it had been just me,

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.980
I wouldn't have been able 
to make them so happy.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.610
That's what I meant by "thanks."

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.920
Wasn't today a great success overall for you?

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.250
Success?

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.740
You're genuinely praising me.

00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:02.700
Could this be a death flag?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.740
Don't put up flags for me. 
I'll break you along with it.

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.020
Good. You're back to normal.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.750
What do you mean, "normal"?

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.900
What's so funny? You're creeping me out.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.950
No, it's just that

00:03:19.950 --> 00:03:23.090
you've never praised my work before.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.100
I'm really happy!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.350
Oh, no. I'm grinning.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.620
What should I do? I can't stop.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.450
Abeno-san?

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.790
Ow!

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.040
There, you stopped.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.020
You just hit me as hard as you could!

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.200
All I did was stop your creepy smiling.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.990
Creepy?! Wh-What are you...

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.250
I'm so sleepy.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.140
<i>I've been doing exorcist work for days on end,</i>

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:57.130
<i>then I go home and do homework 
and help around the shop.</i>

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.140
<i>I guess I'm starting to wear down.</i>

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:00.280
Hanae.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.460
<i>I need to be careful, 
or they'll start calling me</i>

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.420
<i>"Hanae-chan of the Nurse's Office" again.</i>

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:05.990
Hanae.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.890
Yes?

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.140
Huh?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:11.910
Was I hearing things?

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.940
Good morning.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:18.700
Zenko?!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.580
Not so loud.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:20.970
Sorry.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:24.330
Oh, right. We go to the same school, huh?

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.040
How'd you know I was in this class?

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.560
When I was looking for you, 
one of my classmates said,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.840
"You mean Class 2's Hanae-chan 
of the Nurse's Office?"

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.120
Even people in other classes call me that?

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:37.780
Hanae.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:41.210
Thanks for the other day.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.240
I didn't get a chance to thank you then.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.960
It's fine. I did it because I wanted to.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.270
Hey, were you looking for me

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.980
just so you could thank me?

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.600
Oh, right. There's that, too, but...

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.190
Huh?

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.950
Aren't you the girl from Seiryuji Temple?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.950
You're the man in the kimono...

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:11.360
I'm Abeno. Nice to meet you.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.420
Fujiwara Zenko. Nice to meet you.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.590
<i>So she's a high school student.</i>

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.590
<i>So he's a high school student.</i>

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:19.130
It's good that you're here, too.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.040
Huh?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.590
I want to ask you something.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.430
It's this.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.630
Is that a tattoo?

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.360
No.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.830
Those look like teeth marks. 
It looks painful.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.100
It doesn't hurt.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.400
So you guys really can see it.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.750
I showed some other people,

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.570
but they said there was nothing there.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.680
I even got it checked at the hospital,

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.690
but they said there was 
nothing wrong with me.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.700
So if we can see it, that means...

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:55.860
Zenko, look outside the window.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.420
Can you see that?

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.050
<i>It's a yokai.</i>

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:02.660
Hanae,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.170
is that one of the "yokai" you mentioned?

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:07.700
You can see it?

00:06:08.230 --> 00:06:11.210
Yeah. I've been able to see them

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.390
since the day I was bitten by this dog.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.410
A dog?

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.430
The bite came out of nowhere,

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.060
and this mark appeared on my wrist.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.950
That dog was probably a yokai.

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:23.190
What kind of dog was it?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:27.480
Well... There was something 
like smoke coming from it.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.970
And it had big ears.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.200
Well, more than a dog, it was like...

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:33.840
A fox, right?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:42.710
Whoops!

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:44.400
There.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.240
That was a surprise. What's the big idea?

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.210
I could ask you the same thing!

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.130
Who are you?

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:53.890
<i>I didn't sense him at all until he touched me.</i>

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.680
<i>Abeno-san is actually disturbed?</i>

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.880
<i>Could this one be really bad news?</i>

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.360
<i>I had no idea there were yokai in this world</i>

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.150
<i>who could control their power so well.</i>

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.400
<i>It's been at least a hundred years.</i>

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.530
<i>There are still such monsters in this world?</i>

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:14.190
I'm the one who bit the girl, Haruitsuki.

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:14.780
What?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:17.800
"What?"

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.330
Haruitsuki, you forgot about me?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.520
He seems to know you, Abeno-san.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:27.280
Could he have been a 
client of the Mononokean?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.090
If he were, I'd remember.

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:31.660
Well, I suppose it makes sense 
that you don't remember.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.680
You were still small.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:36.250
And I look different now 
from how I did back then.

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:37.690
Did you hear that?

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.540
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:43.160
Even if you don't remember, 
it won't hurt anything.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:46.360
I'm just here to play with you.

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.480
I've been so bored lately.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.860
So won't you play with me?

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.360
Play with you?

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.740
Although...

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:58.620
I don't think you can really 
turn down my invitation.

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.250
Ow!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.210
Zenko!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.970
After all, between letting her arm 
waste away and playing with me,

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.630
it's obvious what you'll choose.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.000
Now then, Haruitsuki,

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.040
why don't we play some hide-and-seek again?

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:21.600
If you beat me, I'll remove the mark on her.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.170
Hide-and-seek?

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:26.100
Yeah, hide-and-seek. 
You know how to play, right?

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:32.280
Really? Don't tell me you 
don't know what it is!

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.490
If you don't know, you can just go away.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.060
I'm not interested in people who 
don't know what hide-and-seek is.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.630
I know what hide-and-seek is!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.750
I used to play it all the time!

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.880
I even played a bunch in middle school!

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:44.250
<i>Middle school?</i>

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.120
<i>He was playing it until just recently?</i>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:49.240
Oh, really? Then there's no problem.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:52.130
I'll hide, so the three of you are "it."

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.160
Okay, then. Ready...

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:54.760
No.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.100
Hanae, Abeno, and I can't play.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:03.100
Why not? Why not?

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.370
What?! No! Let's play!

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.550
No, no, no, no, no!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.580
I won't remove your mark 
unless you play with me!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:14.440
We should do as the fox says so 
you can get your mark removed.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:15.400
No.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.330
No fair!

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.990
Why, why? Why can't you play?

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.990
He's throwing a tantrum.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.400
We can't right now.

00:09:21.400 --> 00:09:22.220
How come?

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.450
Because we have class now.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:26.370
Class?

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:29.180
I don't care about that. Let's play.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:30.020
We can't.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:33.000
If you want us to play with you,

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.470
then wait at my family's 
temple until after school.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.550
We can play lots once I get home.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.010
Aww!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:40.760
Fine.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.090
He's okay with it?

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.020
Good boy.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:46.040
Once class is over, you'd better 
come to the temple right away.

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:46.860
Wait.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.520
What's your name?

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.270
Sorry, but I don't recognize you.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.640
Maybe if I hear your name...

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.530
Try to remember it yourself, Haruitsuki.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:04.860
He's gone.

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.600
I have no idea what he's after.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:14.510
He doesn't seem to want to 
be sent to the Underworld.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:18.590
True. It seemed like he just wanted to play.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.900
But no matter what,

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.510
we need to have him erase 
the mark he put on Zenko.

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:23.420
Yeah.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.890
Then once class is over,

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.610
we'll meet at my place.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:34.020
<b>The Morose Mononokean</b>

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:38.400
<i>Is it because it's nighttime?</i>

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.530
<i>Because this place is deserted?</i>

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.160
<i>I'm getting chills.</i>

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.900
<i>Abeno-san, just answer already!</i>

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.920
<i>And why did it have to be today?</i>

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:55.530
Could someone help me finish 
making some documents today?

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.500
Okay, then. Student number 1, Ashiya!

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:00.300
Yes?

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.900
While we're at it, I'll teach you the 
material from the classes you missed.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.020
Got it?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.780
No regard at all for my own plans?

00:11:06.780 --> 00:11:09.530
I can't today. I have 
something to do after this.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.200
Right, Abeno-san?

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:11.940
Huh?

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.260
You don't have to come.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:17.300
I'll get the hairball to come instead. Just go.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:23.150
<i>He said I didn't have to come, 
but I'm worried, so I came anyway.</i>

00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:27.440
<i>But now I don't know if they're still 
at it or if they worked everything out.</i>

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:29.660
And Abeno-san's not answering his phone!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.320
I should've asked Zenko for her number.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:34.640
Abeno-san! Zenko!

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:37.580
Are you still playing hide-and-seek? Abe—

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.190
I felt something hit my back just now...

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.570
<i>But there's no one there,</i>

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.930
<i>and there's nothing on the 
ground that might've hit me.</i>

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.970
<i>If it were a yokai, I'd be able to see it.</i>

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:53.310
<i>Does that mean it was a ghost?</i>

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:57.040
My back! S-Something's poking my back!

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.730
It's poking! It's poking...

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:00.560
Fuzzy?

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:06.140
Oh, good, it's not a ghost. It's just a yokai.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.840
You don't mind yokai, 
but you can't stand ghosts?

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:10.450
Huh?

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.460
There you are, Zenko!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.820
Over here.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:17.960
Um...

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:21.310
Why are you playing 
hide-and-seek in a graveyard?

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:22.910
Because it's big, apparently.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.720
This is bad luck.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:30.110
It's so dark, I can't tell how far it extends.

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:33.420
Abeno was just walking around here earlier.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:35.220
There he is!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.570
Found you.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:45.360
Huh?

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.740
Aw, shucks. You found me.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.620
The gravestone spoke?!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.950
Abeno-san!

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:56.830
Nice work, Haruitsuki. You found me.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:58.840
But I guess this was too easy.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:02.590
<i>The fox transformed into 
a gravestone to hide?</i>

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.930
Huh? Did you just get here? You're late.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.240
You just finished playing hide-and-seek, huh?

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:12.670
Great. Now we just need you 
to remove Zenko's mark—

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:13.640
One more time!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.770
One more time!

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.910
He escaped? Where did he go?

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.570
He said he'd erase the mark
if we found him!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.520
I've found him zero times, 
Fuzzy found him twice,

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.070
and Abeno found him over 20 times.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.760
Even when we find him, he says 
"one more time," and won't stop playing.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:34.490
That's why Abeno is so exhausted.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.620
We're playing again?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:39.300
So that's why you're dead tired.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:43.090
But now that your hide-and-seek 
veteran is here, we'll be fine!

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:48.490
By the way, Abeno-san, did you 
remember anything about the fox?

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:52.510
No, nothing. But I have 
figured out a few things.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.800
He can hide himself by transforming 
into other things, like he did just now.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:00.040
He's good at concealing his presence.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.760
And just like you, he's incredibly childish.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.040
Please don't glare at me!

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:10.490
In any case, let's play along 
until the fox is satisfied.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:14.240
So we just have to keep finding the fox 
until he doesn't want to play anymore?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:17.040
You're raring to go, Hanae.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.250
By the way, Abeno-san,

00:14:18.550 --> 00:14:21.870
how have you been able to find the fox?

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.580
I wander around the graveyard,

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.260
and when I get close, I can kind of sense him.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:30.490
I see! Wander around the graveyard...

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:38.120
D-Does anyone want to walk around with me?

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.790
Hanae, I can't breathe.

00:14:43.350 --> 00:14:45.120
Are you looking?

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:47.080
I'm looking, I'm looking.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.260
One more time!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.760
We were just walking around there.

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:56.450
I didn't sense anything.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.590
Hey, Abeno-san!

00:14:58.590 --> 00:15:01.670
We can't sense him at all, 
even when we get close!

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.060
Huh? What did you say?

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.420
We can't sense him at all, 
even when we're close!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.210
Just focus!

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.600
He said to focus.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.390
What are we supposed to focus on?

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.370
Maybe like Zen meditation,

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:21.440
we're supposed to clear our minds, 
concentrate, and sharpen our senses.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.880
Or something like that.

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:25.190
Oh! That sounds right.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.830
<i>What was that sensation?</i>

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:39.080
<i>For a moment, I felt like I was 
being drawn somewhere.</i>

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.400
Hanae?

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.740
I think I might know where he is!

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.010
Head straight down this path!

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:47.550
I'm in the lead?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.480
This way, this way!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:49.590
Don't push me.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.620
Let me try again.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:02.440
Hanae...

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.690
Abeno-san!

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:13.950
I just found him disguised 
as a gravestone nearby.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:16.200
We'll capture the yoko.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:20.030
Capture him, huh? I hope 
he doesn't throw a fit.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:22.330
We're not getting anywhere as it is.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.430
We need to try talking to him.

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.190
Abeno-san, you remembered 
the fox's name, then?

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.160
Huh?

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.810
You just called him Yoko.

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.000
That's not his name.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.360
Fox yokai are called "yoko."

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:39.220
Oh... Really?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.470
Why don't you know that?

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:44.230
A servant of the Mononokean ought 
to know at least that much.

00:16:45.140 --> 00:16:46.480
The Mononokean?

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:48.730
<i>"Servant"?</i>

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:53.960
Anyway, I'm going to catch the 
yoko off-guard and capture him.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:56.110
But it's possible he'll try to run.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:17:01.000
So just to be safe, Ashiya, Zenko, and 
Fuzzy, you three hide around the area.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:01.870
Got it.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.980
What's wrong, Hanae?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:07.960
Well...

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.760
I'm not sure...

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.970
Um, I apologize if I'm wrong.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.200
About what?

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.770
Um...

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.770
I found you?

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:30.110
Huh? Why would you think that?

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.440
See? It's not him!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.680
That's not how he'd normally react!

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:35.520
I don't know what "normal" is.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:36.780
I've only met him twice now.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:40.780
Ashiya.

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:43.530
Huh? Now he's reacting like he always does!

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.620
How...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.370
...did you know?

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:50.920
Abeno?

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.650
Aw, shucks. I was pretty confident 
you wouldn't figure it out.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:59.560
I thought I'd have a little fun with you guys

00:17:59.560 --> 00:18:01.680
by transforming into Haruitsuki.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.680
Oh, well. One more time!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.940
Time out! Time out for one second!

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:09.240
Let me go! Let go or I'll bite you!

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:10.690
Abeno-san, I caught the fox!

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:12.700
What? I can't hear you!

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.570
Get over here, please!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.780
What's your problem? Let me go!

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.100
Erase the mark you put on Zenko!

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.120
I'll play with you after you do that!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:25.320
Hanae, I'm surprised you knew the 
fox had transformed into Abeno.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:28.330
Yeah. Something just seemed off.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.320
My transformation was perfect!

00:18:30.320 --> 00:18:31.710
It wasn't how you looked.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:35.090
You called me your "servant," 
but Abeno-san calls me his "employee."

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:38.920
And Abeno-san doesn't call Fuzzy "Fuzzy."

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:40.470
Right?

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:43.050
What does he call him?

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:43.910
Hairball.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.770
There you are.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.650
What are you all doing here?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.650
Abeno, stop.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:51.840
Huh?

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.710
What is this guy's name?

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:54.810
Hairball.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.730
It's true. He's real.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:57.790
See?

00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.600
I won't get it wrong next time!

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:00.490
Huh?

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:04.370
Haruitsuki! Ashiya said 
he won't play anymore!

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.770
Don't lie! I didn't say I wouldn't play!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:10.640
I asked you to remove Zenko's mark first!

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:13.550
You say that, but you'll 
just leave once I erase it!

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:15.900
You have to play with me for three days!

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.010
Three whole days?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.240
In a row?!

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.010
Does he mean to keep playing 
for three days and nights?

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:20.810
Yes! You said you'd play with me lots!

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:23.810
I did, but I didn't mean for three days!

00:19:22.800 --> 00:19:24.890
<i>Play for three days?</i>

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:30.600
Hey, you're the kid from 
the Mononokean, right?

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.070
Let's...

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.520
No!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.190
No! We're going to play! We're playing!

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.880
We can't! We have class!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:41.150
Class again?

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:43.180
If you won't play with me, I won't erase—

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:43.180
Yahiko?

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:45.680
Are you...

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.040
Yahiko?

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:54.040
Haruitsuki, you remembered my name.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.170
Hanae!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.170
He's trying to transform and hide again?!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.430
I'm not hiding.

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:08.380
Whew... Walking on all fours was hard.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:10.930
It took you long enough 
to remember, Haruitsuki.

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:14.560
I just didn't recognize you in your fox form.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:17.530
You've changed, too.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.570
You look totally different now.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:21.870
That was about 30 years ago, right?

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.390
30 years?

00:20:23.390 --> 00:20:26.030
I wasn't born 30 years ago.

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:27.710
It was eight years ago.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:30.950
It was the year I became an 
employee of the Mononokean.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.970
<i>Abeno-san was an employee eight years ago?</i>

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.210
<i>Wait, eight years ago means... He was seven?!</i>

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:40.110
You were working at age seven?!

00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.720
Were you saddled with a debt or something?

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:44.470
I'm not like you.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.900
Haruitsuki, when you were an employee,

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:50.350
the master of the Mononokean was Aoi, right?

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:52.940
<i>Aoi?</i>

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:58.360
And now you're the master of the Mononokean.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.640
Lately I've heard yokai 
spreading rumors about you.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:05.910
I didn't know that in just eight years,

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.410
the master had changed.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:10.550
Yahiko?

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:14.140
Ow!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:15.660
Zenko!

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:16.650
Yahiko, sto—

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:17.670
Haruitsuki...

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:20.170
You haven't changed, right?

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:33.350
Yahiko...

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:40.410
<i>Th-This is that awful feeling I get 
when I'm being possessed by a yokai.</i>

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:46.610
Haruitsuki, I heard another rumor about you.

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:50.640
Is it true that you wanted to be the master,

00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:52.730
so you killed Aoi?

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Time "The Wait"</b>

00:23:26.660 --> 00:23:30.100
You and the fox know each other, huh?

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:30.970
Yeah, I guess.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:35.950
Does that mean you know some raccoon 
dogs, monkeys, and rabbits, too?

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:38.790
What? I'm not a character in a folktale.
